Dependency patch (NOT a vtz source patch) — applied by pin.sh to a LOCAL
CLONE of HowardHinnant/date v3.0.4, because cpp-pkg has no mechanism to
patch a dependency (gap: dep-provisioning; second instance after the absl
patch).

Why: date exports its public HEADERS through target_sources(...
PUBLIC/INTERFACE ...) ("just helps IDEs"), which lands them in the
installed targets' INTERFACE_SOURCES (e.g. date::date-tz carries
include/date/tz.h). CMake never compiles .h entries from
INTERFACE_SOURCES, but cpp-pkg's manifest extraction turns interface
sources into compilable source units and hard-errors:
  error: source `.../include/date/tz.h` has unknown extension `.h`
This is a cpp-pkg extraction bug (headers/unknown extensions in
INTERFACE_SOURCES should be skipped, as CMake itself skips them), worked
around here by removing the IDE-decoration exports. Headers are still
installed via PUBLIC_HEADER, so consumers are unaffected.

pin.sh applies this to a clone of date @ v3.0.4
(f94b8f36c6180be0021876c4a397a054fe50c6f2), commits with pinned identity
+ date (deterministic sha a165a37035b2471ce969a025296e543975b5bdb1), and
rewrites the @DATE_PATCHED_REPO@ placeholder in the staged CppPkg.toml.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index cd0c3f2..5d76ae6 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -72,14 +72,6 @@ add_library( date::date ALIAS date )
 target_include_directories( date INTERFACE
     $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include>
     $<INSTALL_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}> )
-# adding header sources just helps IDEs
-target_sources( date INTERFACE
-    $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/include>$<INSTALL_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}>/date/date.h
-    $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/include>$<INSTALL_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}>/date/solar_hijri.h
-    $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/include>$<INSTALL_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}>/date/islamic.h
-    $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/include>$<INSTALL_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}>/date/iso_week.h
-    $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/include>$<INSTALL_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}>/date/julian.h
-)
 
 set( APPLE_MOBILE_PLATFORM FALSE )
 if ( IOS
@@ -132,9 +124,8 @@ if( BUILD_TZ_LIB )
     add_library( date-tz )
     target_compile_definitions( date-tz PRIVATE BUILD_TZ_LIB=1 )
     target_sources( date-tz
-      PUBLIC
-        $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/include>$<INSTALL_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}>/date/tz.h
       PRIVATE
+        include/date/tz.h
         include/date/tz_private.h
